t many more will dive after we bring (}{\i\f211 we-shall-have-brought}{\f208 ) into the pool\u8230\'c9 the water.\par \par NOTES\par }{\b\f210 1. Hortul}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 nus}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 i}{\f208 , m., }{\i\f211 gardener}{\f208  (derivative of }{\b\f210 h}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 rtus}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 i}{\f208 , m., }{\i\f211 garden}{\f208 ).\par }{\b\f210 2. }{\f208 I}{\b\f210 nquit}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 quoth he (says he)}{\f208 ; pl. i}{\b\f210 nquiunt}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 they say}{\f208 . This verb is not used in all persons.\par }{\b\f210 3. Sp}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 rgo}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 is}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 ere}{\f208  (perfect }{\b\f210 sp}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 rsi}{\f208 ), }{\i\f211 to spread}{\f208 ; }{\b\f210 sp}{\f208 a}{\b\f210 rsus}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 a}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 um}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 having been spread}{\f208 ; derivative: }{\b\f210 consp}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 rgo}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 is}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 ere}{\f208  (perfect }{\b\f210 consp}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 rsi}{\f208 ); p.p. }{\b\f210 consp}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 rsus}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 a}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 um}{\f208  (P. 4).\par }{\b\f210 4. St}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 rcus}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 oris}{\f208 , n., }{\i\f211 manure}{\f208 ; abl. }{\b\f210 st}{\f208 e}{\b\f210 rcore}{\f208  (3}{\f208\super rd}{\f208  declension).\par }{\b\f210 5. Nosocom}{\f208 i}{\b\f210 um}{\f208 , -i}{\b\f210 i}{\f208 , n., }{\i\f211 hospital}{\f208 .\par }{\b\f210 6. }{\f208 Ae}{\b\f210 des}{\f208 , -}{\b\f210 is}{\f208 , f., }{\i\f211 house}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 edifice}{\f208 . This word is mainly used in the plural (ae}{\b\f210 des}{\f208 , gen. ae}{\b\f210 dium}{\f208 ). In the singular it means rather }{\i\f211 temple}{\f208 .\par }{\b\f210 7. Mos}{\f208 , }{\b\f210 m}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 ris}{\f208 , m., }{\i\f211 tradition}{\f208 ; pl. }{\b\f210 m}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 res}{\f208 , }{\b\f210 m}{\f208 o}{\b\f210 rum}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 the mores}{\f208 , }{\i\f211 morals}{\f208 . }{\b\f210 Recent}{\f208 i}{\b\f210